==Trivia==
{{Trivia}}
*The character's last name is probably inspired by the novella [[wikipedia:Heart of Darkness|'Heart of Darkness']] by [[wikipedia:Joseph Conrad|Joseph Conrad]], where a former ivory trader in the Congo named [[wikipedia:Kurtz (Heart of Darkness)|Kurtz]] rules over the native population as a charismatic demigod. The book was later adapted into the [[wikipedia:Vietnam War|Vietnam War]] movie [[wikipedia:Apocalypse Now|'Apocalypse Now']], where [[wikipedia:Walter E. Kurtz|Kurtz's]] assassin is played by [[wikipedia:Martin Sheen|Martin Sheen]] who [[M'Shen]] is likely a reference to. The first name 'Konrad' is probably inspired by the author's last name.
*It is implied in the novel ''[[Lord of the Night (Novel)|Lord of the Night]]'' that Curze had a dual personality. 'He knew that he was two men. One was... just and righteous' - the daemon spat the words, disgusted - 'whilst the other... mm... the other had felt the kiss of Chaos all its life. One thrived on focus. The other ate fear.'{{Fn|1}}
*Also, in the book ''[[Shadows of Treachery]]'', it is revealed that Curze had limited psychic ability, when he destroys a series of lights via a telekinetic pulse.

