Korm (Inquisitor).wikitext:
{{OrdoMalleusPortal}}
'''Korm''' is an [[Ordo Malleus]] [[Inquisitor]].{{Fn|1}}

==History==
He ordered the [[Emperor's Warbringers]] to destroy the [[Imperial]] world [[Vulscus]], after they unknowingly displayed a [[Bolter]] that had once belonged to the traitorous [[Primarch]] [[Horus]]. The population had believed the bolter had belonged to the Primarch [[Guilliman]], who in the world's history had brought Vulscus into [[Compliance]], during the [[Great Crusade]]. However after the bolter was displayed, it was discovered by Korm that the truth had been altered in the wake of the [[Horus Heresy]] and it was Horus who was actually responsible for the Compliance. This led the [[Inquisitor]] to unleash the Warbringers upon Vulscus for their [[heresy]] against the [[Imperium]]. The [[Chapter]] then invaded Vulscus and and Korm accompanied them as they devastated the capital of [[Izo Primaris]], where Horus' bolter was kept. Once they had it in their possession, the Inquisitor wanted to return the bolter to [[Terra]], as he viewed it as a [[Chaos]] artefact of incredible significance. To the Warbringers, though, it was an abomination and they insisted on destroying the ancient bolter. Korm wisely kept silent and did not stop them from doing so, as the Inquisitor did not wish to cross the Chapter.{{Fn|1}}

