Korr.wikitext:
{{SpaceMarinePortal}}{{KhornePortal}}
'''Korr''' is a [[Hawk Lords]] [[Stormtalon]] pilot, in [[Indomitus Crusade Fleet Quartus]]' [[Battle Group Jovia]] and is among its forces that have been corrupted by [[Khorne]]'s [[Murder-Curse]].{{Fn|1}} 
==History==
During the [[Indomitus Crusade]], he served in a [[Stormtalon]] squadron with his [[Hawk Lords]] [[Battle Brother]]s [[Uradus]], [[Voldwyn]] and [[Armandus]] as part of [[Battle Group Jovia|Jovia]]'s '''Task Force IX'''.  It was sent by the Battle Group to reclaim the [[Imperium Sanctus]] world [[Garvetha Primus]] and its [[system]] from [[Heretics]]. The Task Force invaded the world and soon only needed to conquer the city of '''Deng-Var''', to make Garvetha Primus' the [[Imperium]]'s once more. This would then allow the world's system to be opened up for further invasions. However it was as they were fighting to take back the city, that the [[Daemon Primarch]] [[Angron]] destroyed the [[Choral Engine]] on the [[Imperium Nihilus]] world [[Malakbael]], which the majority of [[Indomitus Crusade Fleet Quartus|Fleet Quartus]]' forces had been defending. The [[psychic]] beacon's subsequent explosion, then unleashed [[Khorne]]'s [[Murder-Curse]] [[Warp]] plague, within Malakbael's [[Malak System|system]]. However due to its Battle Groups sharing psychic channels with each other, the Murder-Curse was able to spread to them all, no matter where they were located within the [[Galaxy]].{{Fn|1}}  

Because of this, the [[Warp]] plague soon reached '''Task Force IX''' and those who were infected by it, immediately became servants of the [[Khorne|Blood God]]. Now filled with murderous bloodlust and rage, they fell upon anyone that was near them, including their former allies. While Korr, [[Voldwyn]] and [[Armandus]] all fell victim to it, [[Uradus]] was able to resist the [[Murder-Curse]]. The three infected pilots could somehow sense this though and within moments, Uradus' corrupted [[Battle Brother]]s shot him out of the sky. Korr and Armandus then instinctively formed up upon Voldwyn, as their pack began firing indiscriminately on those fighting beneath them. However Korr would be shot down shortly afterwards, by [[missile]]s fired by one of the Task Force's [[Order of Our Martyred Lady]] [[Exorcist]] [[battle tank]]s. This caused his damaged [[Stormtalon]] to crash into a shrine, where it then exploded within the building.{{Fn|1}}  

==Sources==
*{{Endn|1}}: [[Arks of Omen: Angron]], pgs. 46-49 

