Kortharis.wikitext:
{{NurglePortal}}
[[Image:Kortharis1.jpg|thumb|right|The [[Daemon Prince]] Kortharis{{Fn|2}}]]
'''Kortharis''' is a [[Nurgle]] [[Daemon Prince]], who commands the [[Plaguebones]] [[Chaos Warband|Warband]].{{Fn|1}}
==History==
He was the [[Chapter Master]] of the '''Snakebones''' [[Chapter]], when they clashed repeatedly with the [[Death Guard]] in the [[Subiaco Diablo Sector]] during the [[Eleventh Black Crusade]]. Each time they fought the Death Guard, Kortharis was forced to give the order to retreat after the Snakebones were swarmed with [[Plague Zombies]], used by the [[Traitor Legion]]. He always ensured, however, that the Chapter's [[Apothecaries]] were given enough time to recover their fallen [[Battle Brother]]s' [[Progenoid Glands]]. This proved to be the Snakebones undoing, as the Plague Zombies carried the [[Destroyer Plague]] within them and the harvested Progenoid Glands had been thoroughly infected with the deadly disease.{{Fn|1}} 

When the infected [[Progenoid Gland]]s were later implanted into new members of the '''Snakebones''', the [[Destroyer Plague]] emerged and corrupted the entire [[Chapter]]. In the aftermath of this, Kortharis sought a cure for the Snakebones, but was unable to find one — until the [[Chaos God]] [[Nurgle]] answered his plea for aid. Soon enough, the entire Chapter embraced their new condition and were reborn as the [[Plaguebones]] [[Chaos Warband|Warband]]. Now a loyal servant to the Plague Father, Kortharis has led the Plaguebones against Nurgle's enemies for many battles and has recently ascended to become a [[Daemon Prince]].{{Fn|1}}
==Trivia==
{{Trivia}}
''Kortharis'' and the [[Plaguebones]] were created by the [[Games Workshop]] employee [[Maxime Pastourel]] and they were featured in [[White Dwarf 122 (2016)]]{{Fn|1}}, [[Warhammer: Visions 28]]{{Fn|3}} and [[Warhammer: Visions 29]].{{Fn|2}}
