Kurrinon.wikitext:
{{KhornePortal}}{{WorldEatersPortal}}
'''Kurrinon''' was a [[Berzerker]] of the [[World Eaters]]' [[Foresworn (World Eaters)|Foresworn]] [[Chaos Warband|Warband]].{{Fn|1}}


==Biography==
{{Spoiler|source=It Bleeds (Short Story)}}
He was originally a [[Dragons Ardent]] [[Space Marine Captain|Captain]], with two hundred and sixty years of service to his [[Chapter]] and was also close friends with his [[Battle Brother]] [[Tanikhor]]. However this came to an end sometime after the [[Great Rift]]'s creation, when the [[Foresworn (World Eaters)|Foresworn]] emerged from the giant [[Warp Storm]] and invaded the Chapter's [[Adeptus Astartes Homeworld|Homeworld]] [[Nautilos]]. During the attack, the Chapter thought the walls of its [[Fortress Monastery]] '''Praecipitium''' and their world's deadly waves would allow them to defeat the [[Chaos Warband|Warband]]. In the end, the Foresworn's superior numbers won out and its [[Berzerkers]] breached the Praecipitium's walls and butchered the Dragon's Ardent. Only Kurrinon survived and became despaired when he found the slain body of his friend Tanikhor.{{Fn|1}}  

In keeping with the Dragon Ardent's traditions of claiming the heads of their dead, the [[Space Marine Captain|Captain]] began decapitating his [[Battle Brother]]. As he did so, Kurrinon almost wished he had convinced his [[Chapter Master]] to charge out to meet the Foresworn, so that at least he could have died with his Chapter. The Captain then finished cutting off Tanikhor's head and held it close to him in mourning, as he told his friend that this was not the end. It was then that Kurrinon remembered the [[Feral World|tribal]] population of Nautilos believed that if you held its seashells to your ear, you could hear the demands of their gods. Kurrinon did the same with Tanikhor's lips and suddenly heard the [[Chaos Gods|gods]] speaking to him. The Captain then swore revenge on the Foresworn and vowed to kill as many of them as he could. Kurrinon then left and entered the [[Great Rift]] in pursuit of the Warband, where he began a decades long journey that saw him kill an unknown number of the Foresworn. However during the course of doing so, he became delusional and forgot that his friend had died. This led Kurrinon to begin seeing and speaking to Tanikhor as if he was still alive and the Captain even accepted his counsel on matters. Kurrinon's need for vengeance later led him to fall to [[Heresy]] and he was declared a [[Heretic]] by the [[Imperium]]. He became desperate to save himself afterwards and Tanikhor advised him to join the [[Foresworn (World Eaters)|Foresworn]] for his safety. Though Kurrinon was very reluctant to join the very Warband that had destroyed his Chapter, the imagined Tanikhor convinced him that it was the only way to save himself from the Imperium.{{Fn|1}} 

In order to be accepted by the [[Chaos Warband|Warband]] though, [[Tanikhor]] told Kurrinon he would need to have the [[Butcher's Nails]] implanted within his head. His [[Battle Brother]] then directed the Captain to the [[Chaos Space Marine Apothecary]] [[Bredek]] to have the procedure done. Even as Kurrinon has doubts about going through with it, but Tanikhor is there to continuously convince him, that he has no choice to do so. While Bredek is left wondering who the Captain is talking to, he begins to implant the Butcher's Nails and the operation is a success. Kurrinon then joins the [[Foresworn (World Eaters)|Foresworn]] and losses himself to the madness of the Nails. He fully falls to the worship of [[Khorne]] and even forgets who he was, as he follows the Warband in butchering anyone they come across. The former Captain even comes to believe that he was always a [[World Eater]] and had even took part in the [[Horus Heresy]]'s [[Siege of Terra]]. To the point that Kurrinon vividly remembers seeing the [[Primarch]]s [[Angron]] and [[Sanguinius]] fight within the [[Imperial Palace]]. This delusion holds firm, as he goes on to kill an untold number of [[Imperials]], [[Xenos]] and [[Heretics]] in the Blood God's name.{{Fn|1}} 

Unbeknownst to him, however, a [[Torchbearer Fleet]] had come to [[Nautilos]] sometime after he had left. It had been sent to reinforce the [[Dragons Ardent]], but finding it [[Lost Chapter|destroyed]] instead, the Fleet used its [[Greyshields]] to [[Ultima Founding|Refound]] the [[Chapter]]. The restored Dragons Ardent then carried on the legacy and traditions of their forebears, as they served the Imperium. Eventually, though, word reached them that two members of the original Dragons Ardent had survived the Foresworn's attack and in fact joined the very [[Chaos Warband|Warband]] that had destroyed their Chapter. After learning of this, the Refounded Dragons Ardent's [[Chapter Master]] ordered a group of the Chapter's forces to hunt down the [[Traitor]]s and bring back their heads to him. They would learn of Kurrinon's name and it would be the [[Champion]] [[Su'ul Marhen]] who tracked the Traitor down, as the Foresworn were invading an [[Imperial]] world. After catching Kurrinon by himself, Marhen struck and disarmed the Traitor before knocking him down. The Champion then told the former Captain what had occurred after he left Nautilos and the subsequent rebirth of the Dragons Ardent. Kurrinon was left dumbstruck by all of this, as the use of his name had brought his true past back to him and he remembered everything. Including that his Brother Tanikhor was long dead. Afterwards, Marhen tried to convince Kurrinon to repent his [[Heresy]] by giving the name of the other traitorous Dragons Ardent member. Kurrion refused, however, as he believed it was far too late for him to earn any redemption. As the [[Butcher's Nails]] begin throbbing in his head, Kurrinon instead tells the Champion he was an [[World Eaters|Eater of Worlds]]. This led an exasperated Marhen to execute the former Captain and as he died, Kurrion heard Tanikhor whisper to him that this was not the end. He believes this, for as long as there was vengeance Kurrion would always exist and he knew there was no true end for those who pledge their souls to [[Khorne]].{{Fn|1}}  

==Sources==
*{{Endn|1}}: [[It Bleeds (Short Story)]]

