Kurtiz Mannheim.wikitext:
{{CollegiaTitanicaPortal}}
[[Princeps]] '''Kurtiz Mannheim''' was the temporary commander of the [[Legio Metallica]] [[Titan Legion]] assigned to [[Armageddon]] during the [[Second War for Armageddon]].{{Fn|1}}{{Fn|3}}

==History==
Mannheim was obliged by his oath of loyalty to the [[Emperor of Mankind|Emperor]] to follow an insane order of the corrupted [[heretic]] [[Herman von Strab]], [[Imperial Commander|Overlord]] of Armageddon. Von Strab commanded Legio Metallica to stem the onrushing [[Ork]] tide, even though the [[Imperial]] forces would be outnumbered by more than three to one. Knowing it would be his final mission,{{Fn|3}} Mannheim dressed in his best uniform, said goodbye to his wife and children and climbed aboard his [[Warlord Class Titan]], ''[[Steel Hammer]]'', with pride.{{Fn|1}}{{Fn|3}}

With his Titan critically damaged after destroying three Ork [[Gargant]]s in combat, Mannheim steered ''Steel Hammer'' to the center of the Ork horde and overloaded its plasma reactors, causing a major meltdown and massive explosion. With this action, he took a million Orks with him to the grave.{{Fn|1}} The rest of the Titan Legion was almost completely destroyed by the Orks and took no further part in the campaign.{{Fn|3}}

At the conclusion of the war, Kurtiz Mannheim was posthumously awarded the [[Emperor's Star]] for his mighty deeds. His Titan Legion has been rebuilt and has fought with determination in the [[Third War for Armageddon]], with Mannheim's memory a shining example of the most dutiful and dedicated of warriors.{{Fn|1}} On the planet of Armageddon, he is venerated as a saint by the local populace and has his own holy day, almost as grand as [[Sebastian Yarrick]]'s.{{Fn|3}}

==Notes==
This character has been referred to as both Kurtiz Mannehim{{Fn|2}} and '''Kurt Mannheim'''.{{Fn|1}}{{Fn|2}}{{Fn|3}}

