Kvelter.wikitext:
{{AstraMilitarumPortal}}
'''Kvelter''' is the [[Astra Militarum]] [[General]] of the [[Cadian 2012th]] [[Regiment]].{{Fn|1}} 
==History==
It was among the [[Imperial]] forces that unsuccessfully defended [[Lazulai]] from a [[Tyranid]] invasion. As the world began to fall to the [[Xenos]], after months of warfare, the [[Cadian 2012th]] were among the [[Regiment]]s based in the '''Cobalt Fortress''', which was under Kvelter's command. The Fortress was one of the last left on Lazulai and [[Major]] [[Wulf Khan]], of the [[Catachan CMIII]] which was stationed there as well, believed this was largely due to the General's efforts and skills. Though with Lazulai deemed to be beyond saving, no further reinforcements would be sent to the surviving Imperial forces there. However the world had one asset that was worth saving and [[Lord Commander]] [[Stone (Lord Commander)|Stone]] of [[Sector Command]], ordered General Kvelter to retrieve it. She was not told what the asset was, but Kvelter came to believe it was a weapon that would end the threat of the Tyranids. The invading [[Xenos]] made the mission impossible, though, as each heavily armed group the General sent out from the Fortress, was destroyed before they even came close to the asset's distant location. {{Fn|1}} 

However when an overwhelmingly force of [[Tyranids]] was later discovered to be heading in the direction of the '''Cobalt Fortress''', [[Lord Commander]] [[Stone (Lord Commander)|Stone]] ordered a final attempt to be made to recover the asset. But since their heavily armed groups had been quickly destroyed, Kvelter decided to send out a group that would not be noticed by the [[Xenos]]. The [[General]] would choose [[Major]] [[Wulf Khan]] and her [[Catachan CMIII]] for the mission, as they had the best chance of traversing the hellscape the Tyranids had turned [[Lazulai]] into. Kvelter then told the Major of the mission and that she would be leaving the Fortress with a squadron of her [[Guardsmen]] and an [[Adeptus Mechanicus]] agent-adept, who would oversee the extraction of the asset. They would then head towards '''Opal Bastion''' to meet with an liaison officer from the [[Cadian 82nd]], who would lead them to its location. In order to ensure the best chance for their success, though, the General would draw the Tyranids' attention by advancing towards '''Jasper Fortress'''. Kvelter would lead all of her surviving personnel in the attack, which included the [[Cadian 2012th]] and the remainder of the CMIII. The General and Major both knew how this advance would end, but it would at least give Cobalt's Imperial forces a proper final fight. Major Khan would then salute Kvelter, before leaving to pick her squadron for the mission.{{Fn|1}}

