Laudren Thalarn.wikitext:
{{TzeentchPortal}}{{ThousandSonsPortal}}
{{Fanatic}}
'''Laudren Thalarn''' is a [[Thousand Sons]] [[Sorcerer Lord]], who commands the [[Brothers of Retaliation]] [[Chaos Warband|Warband]].{{Fn|1}}
==History==
He took part in the [[Great Crusade]] and became a mighty [[Chaplain]] in the aftermath of the [[Decree of Nikaea]]. When the [[Thousand Sons]]' [[Primarch]], [[Magnus]], later discovered [[Warmaster]] [[Horus]]' [[Chaos Gods|treachery]], Thalarn convinced many others in his [[Traitor Legion|Legion]], that the [[Emperor]] needed to be warned. However, it was difficult for him to comprehend how Magnus' [[War Within the Webway|efforts]] to do so, led to the Thousand Sons' [[Homeworld]], [[Prospero]], being [[Burning of Prospero|invaded]] by the [[Imperium]]. Thalarn survived the invasion, though, and afterwards, he reluctantly followed his Primarch and the remaining Thousand Sons in joining with Horus' [[Traitor|traitorous]] forces, during the [[Horus Heresy]].{{Fn|1}}

Thalarn would survive the [[Horus Heresy|conflict]] and was among the [[Thousand Sons]] who joined their [[Daemon Primarch|Primarch]], [[Magnus]], on the [[Planet of Sorcerers]]. However, he became extremely bitter about the state of his [[Traitor Legion|Legion]], as many had become hideously [[Mutant|mutated]] and Magnus had become fully corrupted by [[Chaos]]. Thalarn now saw the Thousand Sons as honorless scum, who fought for their mere existence. He blamed their fate on the [[Imperium]] and vowed to never forgive nor forget, how his Legion had been betrayed and humiliated. A thousand years after the Horus Heresy ended, Thalarn fled from the Planet of Sorcerers with hundreds of brothers, who were loyal to him. They then conquered a [[Crone World]] and built the '''Black Cathedral''', which became their base of operations. Once that was done, Thalarn's followers then began recruiting other [[Chaos]] forces to join them. Decades later, he became a powerful [[Sorcerer Lord]] and named his vast [[Chaos Warband|Warband]], the [[Brothers of Retaliation]]. With the numerous forces Thalarn now had at his command, the Sorcerer Lord decided it was finally time to claim his vengeance against the Imperium.{{Fn|1}}
==Trivia==
{{Trivia}}
*''Laudren Thalarn'' and the [[Brothers of Retaliation]] were created by [[Lorens Karaca]]. They appeared in [[The Citadel Journal 33]].{{Fn|1}}

==Sources==
