Lazlo Gratimar Lo Kalligen.wikitext:
{{AstraMilitarumPortal}}
'''Lazlo Gratimar Lo Kalligen''' (service number '''2098231''') was a [[Lieutenant (Imperial Guard)|Lieutenant]] of the [[42nd Paragonian Armoured]] active in the early [[M41|41st millennium]].{{Fn|1b}}


==Biography==
===Early Life===
Back on [[Paragon VI]], Lazlo was born into [[Clan Kalligen]], but was adopted into [[Clan Bannick]] as part of a trade{{Fn|1b}}, becoming a close associate of [[Colaron Vor Artem Lo Bannick|Colaron Artem Lo Bannick]].{{Fn|1a}}{{Fn|1b}} He spent little time learning the customs of the clan, however, as he (correctly) assumed that he was going to land a job in the military and he also developed a reputation as a drinker and a letch.{{Fn|1a}}

Initially Lazlo was going to have a posting in the [[planetary defence militia]]. However, the [[Departmento Munitorum]] called on Paragon to raise a number of [[Imperial Guard Regiment]]s only two weeks after he signed up and Lazlo was drafted into the [[Paragonian Regiments]].{{Fn|1a}}{{Fn|1c}}

===Service===
The 42nd Paragonian Armoured were one of the regiments involved in the [[Kalidar War]], fighting to retake the [[Imperial]] [[Mining World]] of [[Kalidar IV]] from invading [[ork]]s. While fighting on the [[Kostoval Flats]] the Imperial forces were ambushed by the orks and forced to retreat. When the Imperials regrouped at [[Hive Modulus]], Lazlo was missing, presumed dead (due to the [[Death World|harsh]] [[Desert World|desert]] conditions of Kalidar IV).{{Fn|1b}}

