Lazlo Mombril.wikitext:
{{ImperiumPortal}}
'''Lazlo Mombril''' was an [[Imperial citizen]] who lived on [[Sameter]] in early [[M41]].{{Fn|1}}

==Biography==
In '''241.M41''' local authorities found Lazlo mutilated, but alive, on the roof of a disused tannery in the city of [[Urbitane]]. However, although he was rushed to '''Urbitane Mid-rise Sector Infirmary''', Lazlo perished from his injuries 8 minutes after arrival.{{Fn|1}}

It was initially believed that Lazlo, a wandering evangelist, had been the victim of an [[Chaos Cult|heretical Cult]] that was suspected to be behind several murders perpetrated on Sameter over the course of that year. However, an investigation by [[Inquisitor]] [[Gregor Eisenhorn]] (who had been on Sameter following a lead on another case at the time) revealed that there was no such cult - Lazlo and the other victims had been targeted by veteran [[Imperial Guardsmen]] who had returned to Sameter following a long campaign against the forces of [[Chaos]] and, suffering from post-traumatic stress, believed that their victims were heretics and that they were carrying out the [[Emperor]]'s will by purging them.{{Fn|1}}

