'''Lelith Hesperax''', known as the '''Queen of Knives''',{{Fn|3}} is the [[Succubus]] of the [[Wych]] [[Cult of Strife]] and the most famous fighter of the arenas of [[Commorragh]].{{Fn|2}}{{Fn|3}}

===Overview===
Lelith Hesperax is best known for her abilities in the [[Dark Eldar]] coliseums and is considered the undisputed master of the gladiatorial arenas.{{Fn|6}} Instances have been recorded of her fighting and defeating up to ten opponents simultaneously without receiving a scratch. Her preferred combat dress is to expose as much bare skin as she can and to wear her floor-length hair loose in order to taunt her opponents into attacking, a fact that draws significant attention from spectators.{{Fn|2}}

Away from the coliseums of [[Commorragh]] and on the battlefields of the [[M41|41st Millennium]] she is unmatched in hand to hand combat and her speed and skill make her a truly deadly opponent. She will only bless the requests of [[Kabal]]s for aid in [[realspace]] raids when she wishes to seek out unusual prey. She loves to match her abilities against the most formidable champions in the [[galaxy]], and has yet to return without a new clutch of grisly trophies for her private museum.{{Fn|3}}
[[Image:Lelith Hesperax.jpg|thumb|right|220px|Lelith Hesperax{{Fn|2}}]]
Unique amongst most of her kind, Lelith does not use any kind of enhancement drugs for combat. She prefers to fight up close and considers narcotics a sign of weakness. This mindset is usually suicidal for Dark Eldar, and says much about her battle prowess that she remains nearly scarless. Many in Commoragh insist her power comes from a dark source.{{Fn|3}} She is fond of testing herself and putting on grand spectacles, as demonstrated when she turned an entire [[Imperial]] city into a slaughter-arena filled with traps during the [[Battle of Martyr's Rest]].{{Fn|7}}

===History===
Lelith Hesperax was born in a cloning vat owned by the [[Haemonculus]] [[Yukor]]. She along with the rest of her vat-litter were put through brutal training to turn them into future [[Wych]]es for [[Commorragh|Commorragh's]] arenas. Few survived the process, which included battling to the death against [[Wrack]]s with mere shards of metal and wire. Lelith was able to eventually break free of Yukor's control and find her own destiny alongside a handful of others such as [[Morghana Nathrax]].{{Fn|8b}}

After defeating [[Yvraine]] in the arena, Lelith went on to join forces with the reborn prophet of [[Ynnead]], committing much of the Cult of Strife to the [[Ynnari]] effort. This was due to Yvraine curing Lelith of the soul thirst that blights her kind.{{Fn|8a}} Moreover, while many think she simply wishes to erase [[Slaanesh]] with the rest of her kin, in truth she seeks to locate and capture [[Lucius the Eternal]]. Lelith believes that if she can strip Lucius of his daemonic armor and fight him in the arena, it would be the greatest duel Commorragh has ever seen.{{Fn|3}} Lelith Hesperax was one of Yvraine's defenders during the [[Battle of Iathglas]].{{Fn|4}}

Lelith eventually grew bored of guarding Yvraine and with the Ynnari cause in general, and while not cutting ties with them completely she chose to return to Commorragh for a time to pursue new interests. As she departed, the [[Great Harlequin]] [[Prydian Wraitheye]] warned that [[Asdrubael Vect]] had set a trap for her in the Dark City.{{Fn|8a}} Undeterred, upon her and her [[Hekatrix Bloodbrides]] return to Commorragh, she was shocked to discover that the Wych [[Cult of the Thirteenth Night]] under her old rival [[Morghana Nathrax]] had risen to supremacy as Vect's new favored allies over her own Cult of Strife.{{Fn|8b}} 

Lelith eventually is able to meet with Morghana, and she found herself unwilling to attempt to assassinate her during their reunion. While initially dismissive of this, while on a raid against [[Craftworld Eldar]] of [[Ilmaren]] she began to suspect she may have a deeper bond with her due to their shared history.{{Fn|8c}} During the raid, a [[Venom]] attempts to assassinate Lelith, succeeding only in poisoining her with [[Splinter Weapon]] fore. An angry and poisoned Lelith then killed her lieutenant [[Kharavyxis]] to sate her soulthirst. After visiting the [[Haemonculus]] [[Khaebris Kho]] to heal herself, Lelith is still unable to determine who ordered the assassination, though she suspected Vect.{{Fn|8c}}

Seeking distraction in Commorragh's fleshmarkets, Lelith finds herself unexpectedly being worshiped as an idol by the Dark City's abused lower classes. As she speculated that Vect was attempting to have her and Morghana kill one another, she was informed by Prydian Wraitheye that the Cult of the Thirteenth Night was launching an attack on her own palace, the '''Falchion'''. Upon arriving at the Falchion, Lelith was issued a duel challenge by Morghana in Vect's personal auditorium for the title of Queen of the Dark City.{{Fn|8e}} During the subsequent duel, with Vect in attendance, Lelith lost her weapon and Morghana offered her a chance to surrender. However Vect instead ordered Lelith's execution, causing an angry Morghana to unite against Vect. Lelith confronted Vect directly, taking his hand off at the wrist and demanding he cease his shadow war against her. Vect agreed, but subtly warned Lelith against publicly challenging his authority.{{Fn|8f}} Afterwards, Lelith formed a romantic relationship with Morghana and the two agreed to form an uneasy alliance.{{Fn|8g}}

===Wargear===
She is a master of all [[Wych weapons]],{{Fn|1}} but commonly wields a simple pair of wickedly sharp knives.{{Fn|3}}{{Fn|6}} In addition to her conventional weapons, Lelith's hair is sewn through with barbs and hooks, and her fingernails have been honed to scalpel sharpness.{{Fn|3}}

