===Conflicting sources===
====Age and Length of Tenure====
*According to [[Codex: Space Wolves (5th Edition)|the 5th Edition Space Wolves codex]], as of the end of [[M41]], Grimnar has been [[Great Wolf]] for "over 700 years".{{Fn|2a}} However, according to [[Champions of Fenris - A Codex: Space Wolves Supplement|the Champions of Fenris Codex Supplement]], Grimnar was elected Great Wolf in '''440.[[M41]]''', just under 560 years from the end of M41.{{Fn|3}}
*In [[William King]]'s novel ''[[Fist of Demetrius (Novel)]]'', Grimnar is still a young warrior of the Space Wolves at the time of the [[Macharian Crusade]] ('''392-399.M41'''), which is inconsistent with him being Great Wolf for 700 years thereafter, and only slightly less inconsistent with him being elected [[Wolf Lord]] in 415.M41, and Great Wolf in 440.M41.{{Fn|4}}

====Succession====
*Different sources give conflicting information on whom Grimnar succeeded as Great Wolf. The novel ''[[Grey Hunter (Novel)|Grey Hunter]]'' states that the previous Great Wolf was [[Anakron Silvermane]].{{Fn|8}} Later material, however, says that the Great Wolf who preceded Grimnar was [[Sigvald Grimhammer]].{{Fn|3}}

