Loramon Valir.wikitext:
{{OrdoXenosPortal}}
'''Loramon Valir''' is an [[Ordo Xenos]] [[Inquisitor]] who believed that [[Gorgomire]]'s knightly [[Order of the Wyrm]] was in fact a [[Genestealer Cult]] in disguise.{{Fn|1}} 

In order to prove this, Valir and his retinue infiltrated [[Planetary Governor|Governor-King]], [[Archimayn XII]]'s '''Castle Grimheart''', to confront his court magister [[Bargo Xathus]]. Valir suspected Xathus could lead them to the Order's [[Genestealer Patriarch|Patriarch]] and the Inquisitor and his retinue killed any guards that barred their path. As they journeyed further into the Castle, they killed a [[Genestealer]] and found the corrupt dead bodies of the Order, which seemingly showed that the Cult was warring with itself. When they finally neared the court magister's room, however, Valir heard gunfire and raced into the room. He saw another Inquisitor standing over the remains of Xathus. She was [[Sythra Min]] of the [[Ordo Malleus]] and when Valir told her the magister was his jurisdiction, she then exposed a [[Chaos]] symbol on Xathus' body. Thus it was revealed, that there was both a Genestealer and [[Chaos Cult]] active on Gorgomire. The two Cults, though, were now at war with each other and Valir and Min decided to work together to destroy them both.{{Fn|1}}

==Known Retinue==
*'''Alasin''' - [[Interrogator]], who was an [[Enforcer]] until she tried to advance her career by breaking a [[Xenos]] smuggling ring. However, this ended in failure and she then came under the notice of the ring's powerful clients. Only Valir's influence saved Alasin's life and she now strives to repay both the debt she owes and the faith the Inquisitor has in her.{{Fn|1}}
*'''Katrulla''' - Bladeward who claims to be descended from the [[Jovian Void-Clans]]. However the spiraling gang tattoos covering her arms, cause Valir to doubt her claims.{{Fn|1}}
*'''Pirion''' - [[Guardsmen]] deserter whose luck and skills led him to be employed by Valir, before he was found by the [[Officio Prefectus]].{{Fn|1}} 
*The '''Tinkerer''' - [[Jokaero]], who never offered its name and led Valir to call it by what it does best.{{Fn|1}} 
*Two [[Tempestus Scions]], one of which was killed by a [[Genestealer]] on [[Gorgomire]].{{Fn|1}}

