Lortex.wikitext:
{{IronHandsPortal}}
'''Lortex''' is an [[Iron Hands]] [[Techmarine]], who is currently a part of the strike force led by [[Iron Captain]] [[Sind Grolvoch]].{{Fn|1}}
==History==
He is known to be driven by a cold and unshakable belief in his mission and Lortex has heavily modified his body with scores of [[Bionics]]. The [[Techmarine]] uses these replacements, as another means of reaching his goal of achieving greater communion with the [[Chapter]]'s machines. Among his many feats, is that Lortex's whispered prayers hold the power to stir a [[machine spirit|machine's spirit]] to life or unjam a machine's [[bolt weapon]]s. He has also been honored on several occasions, for his cool-headedness in the face of impossible odds. This has led Lortex to be considered the very embodiment of the [[Iron Hands]]' creed, which many of his [[Battle Brother]]s aspire to.{{Fn|1}} 

Perhaps the [[Techmarine]]'s most notable exploit, however, took place during the [[Mechrid Eclipse]], where the [[Iron Hands]] fought an [[Ork]] horde. As the battle raged, the [[Venerable Dreadnought]] [[Rorlaan (Venerable Dreadnought)|Rorlaan]] became immobilized and, after learning of this, Lortex clinically carved his way through a mob of [[Nobz]] in order to reach the Dreadnought. Then, while under heavy Ork fire, the Techmarine made the repairs that allowed Rorlaan to function once more and the Dreadnought proceeded to crush the life out of the horde's [[Warboss|Warlord]]. The Warlord's death caused the Orks to be defeated, but the Iron Hands' victory would have proven impossible, if not for Lortex's heroic actions.{{Fn|1}}

