Lucan Herodas.wikitext:
{{AstraMilitarumPortal}}
'''Lucan Herodas'''{{Fn|1b}} was a [[Imperial Guard Captain|Captain]] of the [[Eighth Pardus Armoured]] [[Imperial Guard Regiment|regiment]] active during the [[Sabbat Worlds Crusade]].{{Fn|1a}}


==Biography==
In the [[Hagia]]n campaign of the Crusade, Herodas was part of a Pardus Eighth detachment led by [[Major]] [[Kleopas]] that was sent to support the [[Tanith First and Only]] and the [[Brevian Centennials]] in the retaking of the [[Holy Doctrinopolis]]. Herodas served as the Pardus' infantry liaison, coordinating with [[Colonel-Commissar]] [[Ibram Gaunt]] of the Tanith First.{{Fn|1a}}

Herodas was later a member of the honour guard assembled by [[Lord General]] [[Lugo]] tasked with retrieving the remains of [[Saint Sabbat]] when the order was given to evacuate Hagia in the face of incoming [[Chaos|enemy]] reinforcements. At one point the honour guard was ambushed by [[Infardi]] [[Chaos Cultist|cultists]]. Although Herodas survived the ambush, he lost his knee to a gunshot and so was sent back to the Holy Doctrinopolis with the rest of the injured; he died from his wounds just before the truck he was in reached the city.{{Fn|1b}}

