Lucian Ventris.wikitext:
{{QuoteBox
|quote = '''''"We commend our souls to the [[Emperor of Mankind|Emperor]]. Let the story of our sacrifice burn across history like a shooting star. For death and for glory - for the Ultramarines!"'''''
|source = - Lucian Ventris, [[Battle for Macragge]], 745.[[M41]].{{Cite this}}
|}}
{{UltramarinesPortal}}
'''Lucian Ventris''' was a [[Veteran Sergeant]] of the [[Ultramarines]] [[1st Company (Ultramarines)|First Company]] who perished at the [[Battle for Macragge]] in 745.[[M41]].{{Fn|1}}{{Fn|2}}  His descendant, [[Uriel Ventris]], also became an Ultramarine, and is the current [[Space Marine Captain|Captain]] of the [[4th Company (Ultramarines)|Fourth Company]].

==Biography==
Like the rest of the First Company, Lucian was detailed to garrison the polar fortresses of [[Macragge]] during the Battle, under the command of Captain [[Saul Invictus]]. The First Company was wiped out to the last man by the attacking [[Tyranid]]s, but their sacrifice kept Macragge secure while [[Chapter Master]] [[Marneus Calgar]] pursued the Tyranid fleet into space and destroyed their [[Hive Ship]]s.{{Fn|1}}{{Fn|2}}

Uriel's descent from a hero of the Ultramarines allowed him to win admission to the prestigious [[Agiselus Barracks]] on Macragge, but he won his induction to the Ultramarines, and his subsequent promotions to [[Space Marine Sergeant|Sergeant]] and [[Space Marine Captain|Captain]] on his own merit.{{Fn|1}}

==Wargear==
Lucian wielded a [[boltgun]], which after his death was reforged into a new boltgun called ''[[Invictus (Boltgun)|Invictus]]''. ''Invictus'' would go on to be wielded by [[Uriel Ventris]].{{Fn|3}}

