Lucien Yavarius-Khau.wikitext:
{{ImperialKnightsPortal}}
'''Lucien Yavarius-Khau''' is the [[High King|High Monarch]] of the [[Knight World]] [[Dominion (Knight World)|Dominion]] and due to its traditions, he commands both [[House Stryder]] and its rival [[House Rau]].{{Fn|1}}
==History==
In [[M42]], [[Dominion (Knight World)|Dominion]] was called upon to send its [[Knights]] to join [[Indomitus Crusade Fleet Tertius]]. When there was no reply to the Imperium's message, it was at first thought that Yavarius-Khau did not receive it, due to the effects of the [[Great Rift]]. In order to make sure that was the case, the Imperium sent the message requesting Dominion's aid twice more. Each time was met with silence from the Knight World, though. Shortly afterwards, however, an embedded spy on Dominion, named [[Tessenna Starne]], learned that an anti-Imperial group had arisen within the two [[Knight House|Houses]]. This group of high ranking Nobles, began talking of seceding from the Imperium and Starne gave her life to ensure a warning of their plot got off-world. It reached the [[Officio Assassinorum]], whose analysis personnel determined that even if Yavarius-Khau was not part of the plot, he should have received the Imperium's messages. The fact that he had not already mustered the Houses to aid Fleet Tertius, meant that the [[High King|High Monarch]] was a secessionist and this warranted his removal by the Assassinorum. [[Execution Force|Execution Force Kingmaker]] was formed for the assassination and after Yavarius-Khau was killed, they were charged with ensuring he was succeeded by a pro-Imperial High Monarch. This way, the Knights of Dominion would have no choice but to aid the [[Indomitus Crusade]] and the Imperium.{{Fn|1a}}

At the midwinter tournament the Execution Force tried to assassinate the High King again as he now openly talked of secession. A bomb goes off during the tournament, which the team uses to get close to the King. As Raithe finally got close enough to fire his [[Exitus Rifle]], it is revealed that the High King has long since been killed, a victim of his own court intrigue.{{Fn|1b}}

The team soon managed to quietly reunite and learned that the Court had been secretly controlling the King for years to avoid civil war as part of a greater conspiracy by traitorous elements.{{Fn|1c}}

