'''Lukas Bastonne''' was a [[Imperial Guard Sergeant|Sergeant]] of the [[Cadian Shock Troopers]]. One of the most recognized faces on [[Cadia]], his image is the public trademark of the [[Cadian]] [[regiment]]s. His heroism and great bravery has earned him enough of reputation that he is instantly recognizable by his superiors, colleagues, and almost the entire population of Cadia. Bastonne's passion for his soldierly duty is second to none, which many whisper borders on fanaticism.{{Fn|1}}

===Biography===
==== Early life and Guard Service====
Bastonne was born into the Cadian nobility which guaranteed him a starting place as an [[Officer]] in the [[Imperial Guard]], but instead of taking the route of a typical noble, Bastonne decided to join at the bottom of the ladder, joining as a [[Private]].  What made Bastonne such an asset to the Imperial Guard was that he has a brilliant memory as well as being a great strategist.  These combined, Bastonne memorizes previous tactical priorities, situations, and his squad's movement, quickly assessing situations - therefore winning victory after victory for the [[Emperor]] and the Imperial Guard wherever he was stationed.  It was not long before he was promoted to Sergeant.{{Fn|1}}

Bastonne has lead his men to many heroic victories such as the '''Defense of Bloodhaven''', the '''Destruction of the Manthral Land-Fortress''' and saving the [[Imperial Governor]] of the [[Imperial]] [[Forge World]] [[Agripinaa]]{{Fn|1}}

====Blessed and Cursed====
Bastonne's prodigious memory is both a blessing and a curse.  Along with the victories he has won, Bastonne also has perfect recall of the many horrors he has seen on the battlefield, and the face and name of every [[Guardsman]] who has served and died under his command.  Though he gives no outward signs of pain or suffering, it is whispered that Bastonne has every one of these names tattooed on his body beneath his uniform.{{Fn|1}}

====Rescue of an Imperial Governor====
Because of his strategic aptitude, Bastonne was called upon to rescue the [[Imperial Governor]] of the [[Forge World]] [[Agripinaa]]. Bastonne and his squad of veterans battled through the plague-ridden streets of the capital [[hive city]] and extracted the Governor.  Yet even after this stunning success, Bastonne, who stubbornly refused to leave any man behind, re-entered the Hive to rescue a wounded trooper, and dragged him to safety.  Bastonne eventually returned home, and all of Cadia was ecstatic at his return.  News of his success was broadcast across the [[Sector]], a parade was thrown in his honour, and Bastonne was awarded the [[Star of Terra]], the highest award any Guard soldier can attain in their lifetime.  Though, not all was as good as it seemed.{{Fn|1}}

What was never made public during the massive celebrations was that the trooper Bastonne had gone back to rescue had become infected by Chaos, and Bastonne had been forced to execute him on the voyage home - another face to haunt him during his restless nights.{{Fn|1}}

====13th Black Crusade====
Bastonne stood at the forefront of [[Cadia]]'s defense, during the [[13th Black Crusade]]. He later became an [[Imperial]] martyr whilst holding back [[Abaddon the Despoiler]]'s invading [[Chaos]] forces,{{Fn|2}} which led to Bastonne's death at the hands of a [[Sorcerer]]. Though his [[Regiment]] kept his [[Astra Militarum Honours|medals]], Bastonne's commanding officer, [[Colonel]] [[Devere]], honored the [[Imperial Guard Sergeant|Sergeant]]'s final instructions and sent his [[power sword]] to [[Lord Castellan]] [[Ursarkar E. Creed]].{{Fn|3}} 

When [[Ursarkar E. Creed|Creed]]'s [[Colour Sergeant]], [[Jarran Kell]], later presented the [[power sword]] to him, the [[Lord Castellan]] recognized that it was Bastonne's weapon. Kell then told Creed of how the [[Imperial Guard Sergeant|Sergeant]] died in battle on [[Cadia]]'s southern curtain wall, but the Lord Castellan immediately refused to accept the power sword. Instead, Creed ordered the Colour Sergeant to send it back to Bastonne's [[Regiment]] with his condolences. Kell refused and chided the Lord Castellan by telling him it was Bastonne's final request that the weapon be given to Creed. The Sergeant had also stated that the Lord Castellan could do what he wanted with the power sword and Kell recommended placing the weapon in the [[Cadian 8th]]'s [[Regiment|regimental]] chapel or the '''Museum of Resistance'''. Upon hearing this, Creed took the power sword and thanked Kell for giving it to him.{{Fn|3}} 

However when [[Abaddon the Despoiler]] later dealt [[Cadia]] a [[13th_Black_Crusade#Fall_of_Cadia|death blow]], the [[Imperium]] was forced to evacuate the [[Fortress World]].{{Fn|3}} The [[Imperial Guard Sergeant|Sergeant]]'s weapon, though, was among the items taken to safety and it became known as [[Bastonne's Sword]]. The weapon is now a relic of Cadia and acts as a symbol of defiance in defense.{{Fn|2}}

