Luthar Hewall.wikitext:
{{ImperiumPortal}}
'''Luthar Hewall''' was a rug-maker who lived and worked in the city of [[Urbitane]] on the planet [[Sameter]]. He was one of the victims of a string of serial murders that swept Urbitane in the year '''241.[[M41]]'''.{{Fn|1}}

==History==
He was last seen alive on the 24th of Aquiarae (by Sameter's local calendar). He had delivered a finished rug to a high-rise apartment building, then proceeded to meet up with some friends for a meal in a mid-rise charcute.{{Fn|1}}

Hewall's body was found in one of Urbitane's soil stacks in early Sagittar (the next month) by sanitation maintenance workers. An examination of the corpse suggested that the killers had tried to burn Hewall's body after his death, and then disposed of his remains using the sewage system. In addition, the corpse was missing a number of its extremities. However, due to the advanced state of decay (exacerbated by the filthy soil stack) the post-mortem was inconclusive on the exact cause of the missing body parts; the investigators believed that it was possible that these had rotted away in the time before the body was found, however a number of marks on the ends of the forearm bones were suggestive of a saw or [[chainblade]].{{Fn|1}}

More information was uncovered when a second corpse was found - that of a midwife called [[Idilane Fasple]] - that had been mutilated in a similar manner to Hewall's. The city's [[Arbites]] concluded that both victims had been killed by the same perpetrator. They were later able to link [[Poul Grevan|another recent death]] to the spate of killings.{{Fn|1}}

Both Captain [[Hurlie Wrex|Wrex]] and Minister [[Eskeen Hansaard|Hansaard]] believed that the ritualistic nature of the murders indicated the presence of a [[Chaos Cult|heretic cult]] active in Urbitane. Following an investigation by [[Inquisitor]] [[Gregor Eisenhorn]], however, he determined that the "cultists" were in fact veteran [[Imperial Guardsmen]] who, afflicted with [[Battle of Klodeshi Heights|severe shellshock]], believed that their victims (including Hewall) were heretics and executed them.{{Fn|1}}

==Sources==
*{{Endn|1}}: [[Missing in Action (Short Story)]]

